      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the explanation! That makes things more clear. From your description, the `mDirectOpenCount` increasment indicates that it is a shared stream. If the `mDirectOpenCount` remains 1 indicates that `stopOutput` is not called correctly. \n\nBack to the code, from my understanding, this CL wants to set `mPortId` as `NONE` from method `disconnect` and then call `stopOutput` when calling `start` and `mPortId` is `NONE`. AFAIK, the `disconnect` method will only be called when the MmapThreadHandle is destroyed. See [code](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/services/audioflinger/Threads.h;l\u003d2236;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d1). In that case, if `MmapThread::start` is called after `MmapThread::disconnect` is called, it is a severe problem as we are calling to something that is already destroyed or is destroying.\n\nThat sounds like a race condition that the mmap interface is freed when `start` method is not yet finished. Given the report is on a U code base, I will double check if this is already fix on latest build or not.\n\nBut the change of sending an error callback if the callback thread cannot be created is still needed.",
      "parentUuid": "7d6910c2_c0b1c159",
